course: dictionary
lesson: 5390
title: Known and well-known
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Known is a form of the word know. You use it after have or be: «I have known her for years.» «It is known.» Here known means people have found it out or have it in their minds.
explain: As an adjective, known means already found out, so it is not a mystery. «There are 118 known elements» means 118 elements that scientists have already found and named.
explain: Well-known means famous, known by many people. A «well-known song» is one that lots of people have heard. Look at the words around known to check which meaning it has.
fact: Known is the form of know used after have or be.
fact: As an adjective, known means already found out or named by people.
fact: Well-known means famous, known by many people.
fact: «Unknown» is the opposite of known.
fact: «Saturn has the most known moons of any planet, more than 270, and the count is still rising.»
exercise: In «I have known her for years», known is a form of which word? | *know | knowing | knew | knows
exercise: «The Amazon basin has well over two thousand known kinds of fish.» What does known mean here? | Swimming in groups | Very old and rare | *Found out and named by people | Hidden under the water
exercise: What does well-known mean? | Very small | Lost for a long time | Frightening | *Famous, known by many people
test: A «well-known song» is best described as: | A song that nobody has heard | *A song that many people know | A song written a very long time ago | A song sung by only one person
test: Which word is the opposite of known? | known as | make known | *unknown | well-known
exam: Which sentence uses known as an adjective meaning already found out? | *«There are 118 known elements.» | «He will knew the answer soon.» | «Her knowing smile made us laugh.» | «She knows the way home.»
